<h2 class="vetrina-section-title">Features</h2>

<div class="vetrina-grid">
  <div class="vetrina-grid-content">
    <p class="vetrina-intro-text">
      FakeData is built for developers who need realistic test data fast.
    </p>

    <ul class="vetrina-features-list">
      <li><strong>80+ generators</strong> — People, geography, web, time, types, and fun categories</li>
      <li><strong>Multiple formats</strong> — Tab-separated, CSV, or NDJSON output</li>
      <li><strong>Streaming mode</strong> — Generate data indefinitely for load testing</li>
      <li><strong>Templates</strong> — Custom output with Go templates (JSON, YAML, any format)</li>
      <li><strong>Deterministic</strong> — Use seeds for reproducible results every time</li>
      <li><strong>Shell completion</strong> — Bash, zsh, and fish support</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="vetrina-grid-terminal">
    <div class="terminal-window">
      <div class="terminal-header">
        <span class="terminal-dot red"></span>
        <span class="terminal-dot yellow"></span>
        <span class="terminal-dot green"></span>
        <span class="terminal-title">bash</span>
      </div>
      <div class="terminal-body">
        <div class="terminal-comment"># Custom output with templates</div>
        <div class="terminal-line">
          <span class="terminal-prompt">$</span> fakedata -T user.tmpl -n 2
        </div>
        <div class="terminal-line terminal-output">{"name": "John Doe", "email": "john@example.com"}</div>

        <div class="terminal-comment"># JSON output</div>
        <div class="terminal-line">
          <span class="terminal-prompt">$</span> fakedata -f ndjson -n 2 name email
        </div>
        <div class="terminal-line terminal-output">{"name": "Jane Smith", "email": "jane@test.com"}</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

